# Agent may build and run test binaries

Agents **may** compile, link, and run product/test binaries when fixing build or test failures, or when a skill (`auto-build-fix`, `auto-bug-fix`, `auto-idle-pipeline`) requires it.

## Preferred entry

From the **smartgis** repo root:

```bat
.\build.bat
.\build.bat debug
.\build.bat debug te
.\build.bat e2e
.\build.bat <single_target>
```

Prefer `build.bat` over bare `gn` / `ninja` unless fixing the entry itself. Gen roots are **`out/Debug`** and **`out/Release`** (see `.cursor/rules/build/build-output.mdc`). For a faster agent loop, prefer **`build.bat debug …`**.

**Multi-conversation lock:** **default OFF**. Agents **must not** enable it (`out/.build.lock.on` / `SMARTGIS_BUILD_LOCK=1` blocked by `.cursor/hooks/build_lock_gate.py`). Prefer `build.bat debug <single_target>` and non-overlapping paths. See **`.cursor/rules/build/build-lock.mdc`**.

## Allowed

- `build.bat` (any argument, including `debug` / `release`, `te`, `e2e`, `m`, `a`, `b`, or a single target)
- `gn`, `ninja` only when diagnosing/recovering the GN entry itself (still respect per-config locks; prefer waiting on `build.bat`)
- Product / test binaries under `out\Debug\` or `out\Release\` (e.g. `*_test.exe`, `exe_smoke.exe`, `SmartGIS.exe --self-test`)

## Still forbidden

- `SmartGIS.sln` / MSBuild / `build.bat sln` as the fix loop (`vs2008/` is leftover only)
- Bare `out/` or `out/Default` as a gen root; inventing a second install root
- Parallel bare `ninja` on the **same** `out/Debug` or `out/Release` while another conversation holds that scope

## Skills

When `@auto-build-fix` / `@auto-bug-fix` / `@auto-idle-pipeline` is attached or invoked, follow that skill’s loop: run the build/tests, parse logs, fix root cause, re-run until the done bar.
